Dirijor / Diri (https://github.com/cristicretu/diri)
----------------------------------------------------
Ubra is a renamed derivative of the Apache-2.0 open-source project Diri, which
was itself named Dirijor. Its source, documentation (including the contributor,
privacy, security, roadmap, Linux and agent-manifest documents), agent
manifests, vendored dependency patches, and third-party attributions were the
starting point of this workspace. Changes made: the project, crate, binary and
bundle names were changed to ubra, path prefixes were flattened to the
repository root, and the product code has since diverged. Copyright (c) the
Dirijor/Diri contributors.
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; a copy of the license is
available at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Ubra is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or
endorsed by the Diri project or its maintainers, and it uses the Diri name only
to describe the origin of this work.

Provenance and change statement: this workspace was imported as a single
snapshot of the Diri workspace with the paths, crate names, binary names and
bundle identifiers renamed to ubra. Files that were not otherwise touched remain
verbatim apart from that rename; no per-file notice is carried. This file and
`README.md` are the notice of those changes, and they apply to every file in the
repository.

GPUI (https://github.com/zed-industries/zed)
--------------------------------------------
Copyright 2022 - 2025 Zed Industries, Inc. — the Apache-2.0 license text
shipped with the pinned revision carries that notice, reproduced here so
distributed binaries keep it.

The GPUI crates used by Ubra are pinned to a specific Zed revision. Crates
marked Apache-2.0 by upstream remain under that license. Zed describes its
repository as primarily GPL-3.0-or-later with Apache-2.0 components where
marked; the dependency inventory is checked by `scripts/check-licenses.py`.

No GPL-licensed code is linked into Ubra's binaries. Two crates in the graph
declare no license field (`gpui_util`, `gpui_shared_string`); each ships its
own Apache-2.0 `LICENSE-APACHE` inside its crate directory, and crates.io
publishes `gpui_util` under Apache-2.0. `scripts/license-policy.json` records
that evidence.

Ubra replaces GPUI's disabled, no-op `ztracing` profiling surface with a small
independent Apache-2.0 compatibility implementation in `vendor/` so the
unused GPL logging/profiling implementation is not linked into release builds.

The vendored `gpui_macos` renderer is an Apache-2.0 component from the same
pinned revision, with the local changes described in `Cargo.toml` and
`vendor/gpui_macos/README.ubra.md`; the `gpui` cache fix is described in
`vendor/gpui/UBRA_PATCHES.md`.

