herdr (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr)
-----------------------------------------
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr/blob/master/LICENSE). The upstream LICENSE
file names no copyright holder (it ships the Apache-2.0 template with
`Copyright [yyyy] [name of copyright owner]` unfilled and carries no NOTICE
file), so this entry attributes `herdr contributors
(https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr), Apache-2.0` rather than inventing a name.
A copy of the license is available at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The screen-detection predicates in the following files are ADAPTED from
herdr's TOML screen manifests (`src/detect/manifests/*.toml`):

    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/amp.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/antigravity.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/cline.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/copilot.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/devin.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/droid.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/grok.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/hermes.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/kilo.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/kimi.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/kiro.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/maki.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/opencode.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/pi.json
    crates/ubra-engine/manifests/qoder.json

Changes made: the rules were translated from herdr's TOML rule schema into
Ubra's JSON predicate schema, re-prioritised for Ubra's evaluator (which
stops at the first matching rule by descending priority), restricted to the
screen regions Ubra implements, and paired with capture regions. Rules that
depend on herdr-only regions (`top_non_empty_lines`, `after_last_horizontal_rule`,
`after_last_prompt_marker`) were dropped rather than approximated.

The `"agent"` capability blocks in those files — binaries, resume specs,
session-id flags, approve/deny keystrokes, env hygiene, injection wiring — are
Ubra's own; herdr does not model most of them. Binary names and resume
argv were cross-checked against herdr's `src/detect/mod.rs` and
`src/agent_resume.rs`.

The manifests for claude-code, codex, cursor, generic, shell, and the other
Ubra-owned agents predate this attribution.

