Terminal color schemes
----------------------
The bundled terminal palettes in `crates/ubra-term/src/theme.rs` reproduce
published third-party color schemes:

    Solarized       https://github.com/altercation/solarized — MIT
    Dracula         https://github.com/dracula/dracula-theme — MIT
    One Dark        https://github.com/atom/atom — MIT
    Gruvbox         https://github.com/morhetz/gruvbox — MIT (declared in its
                    package.json and README License section)
    Tokyo Night     https://github.com/tokyo-night/tokyo-night-vscode-theme — MIT
    Catppuccin      https://github.com/catppuccin/catppuccin — MIT
    Nord            https://github.com/nordtheme/nord — MIT
    Rosé Pine       https://github.com/rose-pine/rose-pine-theme — MIT
    Kanagawa        https://github.com/rebelot/kanagawa.nvim — MIT
    Everforest      https://github.com/sainnhe/everforest — MIT
    GitHub Light    https://github.com/primer/github-vscode-theme — MIT
    Vesper          https://github.com/raunofreiberg/vesper — MIT

All twelve schemes are used under their upstream MIT terms; the MIT license
text is reproduced in `docs/third-party/MIT-microsoft-terminal.txt`.

Each palette remains the work of its authors and is used under that project's
own terms; the palettes are reproduced as color values, not copied source
files. Vesper's ANSI colors come from its upstream Warp theme, and its cursor
and selection colors from its iTerm profile. `Ubra Dark` and `Ubra Light` are
Ubra's own.

